<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      Android hardware-abstraction implementation of the interfaces
      declared in Cassam.Ui.Hardware.Common.

      TFM: net10.0-android — matches the Uno Platform 6 Android head
      (`net10.0-android` API 36, see Cassam.Ui.csproj). The android
      workload is already installed on the dev host per PR 6, so the
      build verifies here.

      What lives here (T2.05 per PR 7 user instructions; design §6.2
      "Android" row):
        - AndroidBarcodeScanner — USB-OTG HID (Android USB Host API,
              `UsbManager`) + Bluetooth HID / SPP (Plugin.BLE). Most
              retail Android scanners pair over Bluetooth (the
              Android scanner market has converged on BT-SPP and
              BT-HID).
        - AndroidEscPosReceiptPrinter — BT SPP / BLE GATT write
              characteristic (Plugin.BLE). BT is the common Android
              path; USB-OTG is rare on Android POS tablets.
        - AndroidBluetoothCashDrawer — kicks via the paired BT printer
              (the standard "drawer piggy-backs on the printer RJ12
              cable" wiring used by every mobile POS in LATAM).
        - AndroidBluetoothPoleDisplay — BT serial (rare in retail but
              declared for forward-compatibility, design §6.2 row 4).
        - AndroidHardwareModule.AddAndroidHardware(services) — DI
              extension.

      Out of scope for PR 7 (deferred):
        - Ambient-light sensor triggering HighContrastTheme at
          > 25 000 lux (design §6.2 row 4 note). Lands with the
          Android head's theme system in PR 8.
        - USB-OTG ESC/POS printer path — same Plugin.BLE BT path
          covers 99 % of Android retail in LATAM.

      Risk acknowledgment (design §16 R-UI-06): Android BT pairing
      UX varies by OEM (Samsung vs Xiaomi vs motorola). The HAL
      abstracts pairing behind the IBarcodeScanner.StartAsync
      surface; the actual pair-on-first-scan UI lands in the
      cashier flow (PR 8).

      Plugin.BLE is MIT-licensed — see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md (TBD
      in PR 8 alongside the WASM camera fallback that lands at the
      same time).
    -->
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-android</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <RootNamespace>Cassam.Ui.Hardware.Android</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Cassam.Ui.Hardware.Android</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Cassam.Ui.Hardware.Common\Cassam.Ui.Hardware.Common.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Plugin.BLE" Version="3.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
